  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>b</mi></math> respectively be the semi-transverse and semi-conjugate axes of a standard hyperbola whose eccentricity satisfies the equation <math><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If <math><mi>S</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is a focus and <math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> is the corresponding directrix of this hyperbola, then <math><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "equPO",
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tFz5T",
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ycdcs",
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "apvIl",
      "text": "<math><mn>7</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given that focus of hyperbola is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mn>, 0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br /><br />Therefore, Directrix&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>e</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; ......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math><br /><br />From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math>, we get&nbsp;<math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>(It satisfies <math><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> )</p><p>We also know that for an ellipse,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p>",
